This is a very basic video editing application. The application will be used to
cut ads from a video recorded from tv. The app won't reencode the streams, it
will just allow to cut part of the streams and for this reason every remaining
clip will begin from a full frame. Clips can end wherever they want. The
application will be a graphical application that will allow to navigate the
video, both from full frame to full frame and from intermediate frame to
intermediate frame and select which video and audio streams to export.

mkv will be the ending container, while input file could be at least in .ts and
.mkv format. Input should support all codecs used in DVB-T and DVB-T2
standards. Support for other containers and codecs would be nice to have, but
not necessary.

The application should work well in Linux and Wayland.

Future improvements:
- a tool to help finding ads;
- a feature to automatically detect and remove ads.

The application should aim to use as few dependencies as possible, but it's ok
to use a media handling library (like ffmpeg for example). The choice of the
language is not relevant.
